          "subject": "fix(core): resolve DeepSeek's official API `deepseek-flash` name at V4 limits (#11909)",
          "parents": [
            "156092e892db5b098bd6d0ecf606dd37449538fe"
          ],
          "body_excerpt": "The official DeepSeek API only accepts `deepseek-flash` and `deepseek-v4-pro`\nas model names, but the V4 rules keyed on `/^deepseek-v4/`, so the direct-API\nname fell through to the generic 128K/32K row and long sessions died on\nCOMPRESSION_FAILED_OUTPUT_TRUNCATED. Both rules now match\n`/^deepseek-(?:v4|flash)/`; older families keep their pinned fallbacks.\n\nCloses #11894"
        },
